<title>USA: American Bankers splits stock, raises div.</title>
<headline>American Bankers splits stock, raises div.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Bankers Insurance Group Inc said Friday it had declared a two-for-one stock split and increased its quarterly dividend.</p>
<p>The split is payable September 12, record August 29.</p>
<p>The new quarterly dividend is $0.22 on current shares, or $0.11 on a post-split basis. The company previously paid $0.21 a share.</p>
<p>&quot;The board's approval of the stock split is a move to increase liquidity and ownership by making the stock accessible to a wider range of investors,&quot; a company statement said.</p>
</text>
